From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:24:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 130/141] tslp4: the record case fails on its own

Sum accumulated into its result, a store the caller sees, which kept every
load of the loop in place, so the record case passed even where the field
was hoisted. It accumulates in a local now: it fails when only record
fields are moved again, as the array case does for array fields.
---
 tests/test/opt/tslp4.pp | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test/opt/tslp4.pp b/tests/test/opt/tslp4.pp
index 8c6068d6..8af445eb 100644
--- a/tests/test/opt/tslp4.pp
+++ b/tests/test/opt/tslp4.pp
@@ -43,13 +43,16 @@ begin
   result := false;
 end;
 
+{ the loop accumulates in a local: a store to the result is visible to the
+  caller, so it would keep every load in the loop and hide the record case }
 function Sum(P: POuter): LongInt;
 var
-  I: LongInt;
+  I, S: LongInt;
 begin
-  result := 0;
+  S := 0;
   for I := 0 to P^.Inner.Count - 1 do
-    inc(result, P^.Inner.Items[I]);
+    S := S + P^.Inner.Items[I];
+  result := S;
 end;
 
 procedure check(ok: boolean; const what: string);
